{"documents":[{"entities":[{"text":"Steve Jobs","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"Apple","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"1976","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Tim Cook","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"iPhone","type":"TECHNOLOGY"},{"text":"iOS","type":"TECHNOLOGY"}],"id":"apple","relations":[{"source":"Steve Jobs","target":"Apple","type":"founded_by"},{"source":"Tim Cook","target":"Apple","type":"works_for"},{"source":"Apple","target":"iPhone","type":"developed"}],"text":"Steve Jobs founded Apple in 1976. Tim Cook works for Apple as its chief executive. Apple developed the iPhone, a smartphone that runs iOS."},{"entities":[{"text":"Larry Page","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"Sergey Brin","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"Google","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"1998","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Mountain View","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"California","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"PageRank","type":"TECHNOLOGY"},{"text":"YouTube","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"2006","type":"DATE"}],"id":"google","relations":[{"source":"Larry Page","target":"Google","type":"founded_by"},{"source":"Sergey Brin","target":"Google","type":"founded_by"},{"source":"Google","target":"Mountain View","type":"located_in"},{"source":"Google","target":"California","type":"located_in"},{"source":"Google","target":"PageRank","type":"developed"},{"source":"Google","target":"YouTube","type":"acquired"}],"text":"Larry Page and Sergey Brin founded Google in 1998. Google is headquartered in Mountain View, California. Google developed PageRank and later acquired YouTube in 2006."},{"entities":[{"text":"Satya Nadella","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"Hyderabad","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"India","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Microsoft","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"1992","type":"DATE"},{"text":"2014","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Redmond","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Washington","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Windows","type":"TECHNOLOGY"}],"id":"microsoft","relations":[{"source":"Satya Nadella","target":"Hyderabad","type":"born_in"},{"source":"Satya Nadella","target":"Microsoft","type":"works_for"},{"source":"Microsoft","target":"Redmond","type":"located_in"},{"source":"Microsoft","target":"Washington","type":"located_in"},{"source":"Microsoft","target":"Windows","type":"developed"}],"text":"Satya Nadella was born in Hyderabad, India. He joined Microsoft in 1992 and became the CEO of Microsoft in 2014. Microsoft, based in Redmond, Washington, developed the Windows operating system."},{"entities":[{"text":"Sam Altman","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"OpenAI","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"ChatGPT","type":"TECHNOLOGY"},{"text":"large language model","type":"TECHNOLOGY"},{"text":"2022","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Microsoft","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"Azure","type":"TECHNOLOGY"}],"id":"openai","relations":[{"source":"Sam Altman","target":"OpenAI","type":"works_for"},{"source":"OpenAI","target":"ChatGPT","type":"developed"},{"source":"OpenAI","target":"Microsoft","type":"partner_of"}],"text":"Sam Altman is the CEO of OpenAI. OpenAI developed ChatGPT, a large language model released in 2022. OpenAI partnered with Microsoft to run ChatGPT on Azure."},{"entities":[{"text":"Alan Turing","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"London","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"1912","type":"DATE"},{"text":"1936","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Grace Hopper","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"New York","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"1906","type":"DATE"},{"text":"1952","type":"DATE"}],"id":"computing pioneers","relations":[{"source":"Alan Turing","target":"London","type":"born_in"},{"source":"Grace Hopper","target":"New York","type":"born_in"}],"text":"Alan Turing was born in London in 1912. He published the concept of a universal machine in 1936. Grace Hopper was born in New York in 1906. She developed the first compiler in 1952."},{"entities":[{"text":"Elon Musk","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"SpaceX","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"2002","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Hawthorne","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"California","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Tesla","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"Austin","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Texas","type":"LOCATION"}],"id":"musk companies","relations":[{"source":"Elon Musk","target":"SpaceX","type":"founded_by"},{"source":"SpaceX","target":"Hawthorne","type":"located_in"},{"source":"SpaceX","target":"California","type":"located_in"},{"source":"Elon Musk","target":"Tesla","type":"works_for"},{"source":"Tesla","target":"Austin","type":"located_in"},{"source":"Tesla","target":"Texas","type":"located_in"}],"text":"Elon Musk founded SpaceX in 2002. SpaceX is headquartered in Hawthorne, California. Elon Musk also leads Tesla, an electric vehicle company based in Austin, Texas."},{"entities":[{"text":"Marie Curie","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"Warsaw","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Poland","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"1867","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Pierre Curie","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"Paris","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"1898","type":"DATE"}],"id":"curie","relations":[{"source":"Marie Curie","target":"Warsaw","type":"born_in"},{"source":"Marie Curie","target":"Poland","type":"born_in"}],"text":"Marie Curie was born in Warsaw, Poland, in 1867. Working with Pierre Curie in Paris, she discovered radium in 1898."},{"entities":[{"text":"IBM","type":"ORGANIZATION"},{"text":"1911","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Armonk","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"New York","type":"LOCATION"},{"text":"Watson","type":"TECHNOLOGY"},{"text":"2011","type":"DATE"},{"text":"Ginni Rometty","type":"PERSON"},{"text":"2012","type":"DATE"},{"text":"2020","type":"DATE"}],"id":"ibm","relations":[{"source":"IBM","target":"Armonk","type":"located_in"},{"source":"IBM","target":"New York","type":"located_in"},{"source":"IBM","target":"Watson","type":"developed"},{"source":"Ginni Rometty","target":"IBM","type":"works_for"}],"text":"IBM, founded in 1911, is headquartered in Armonk, New York. IBM developed Watson, a question answering system, in 2011. Ginni Rometty served as CEO of IBM from 2012 to 2020."}],"labeling_notes":"Gold labels were written by hand for this set. Entities use the surface form as written in the text. Relations use the eight relation types the system supports, in the direction conventions documented in knowledge_graph_explorer/llm_extractor.py. A located_in label is included for both a city and its state when the text states the location as a city, state pair. See eval/README.md for the full labeling rules.","name":"knowledge-graph-explorer extraction eval, version 1"}